From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Guard the optional secondary read value

Most fault decoders pass NULL for value2 because only a 16-byte read needs a
second result.  Keep its initialization for that path without dereferencing
NULL on ordinary reads before the Bellatrix machine hook is reached.
---
 src/aarch64/vectors.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/aarch64/vectors.c b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
--- a/src/aarch64/vectors.c
+++ b/src/aarch64/vectors.c
@@ -833,7 +833,8 @@ int SYSReadValFromAddr(uint64_t *value, uint64_t *value2, int size, uint64_t far)
     D(kprintf("[JIT:SYS] SYSReadValFromAddr(%d, %p)\n", size, far));
 
 #ifdef BELLATRIX_EMU68
-    *value2 = 0;
+    if (value2)
+        *value2 = 0;
     if (machine_bus_read((uint32_t)far, size, value))
         return 1;
 #endif
-- 
